WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.450
One drop of blood, on a cheap paper strip.

2
00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:06.720
Within seconds or
minutes, the pad darkens.

3
00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:09.970
The darker it gets, the
more glucose in the drop.

4
00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:14.100
People with diabetes use strips like
this to check their own blood glucose at

5
00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:15.070
home.

6
00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:20.060
So how can a cheap paper strip measure
the sugar in a single drop of blood?

7
00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:23.320
In this mission, you'll see
how enzymes found in blood,

8
00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:27.240
urine or sputum help
doctors diagnose disease.

9
00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:30.160
Then you'll trap an
enzyme inside gel beads,

10
00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:32.910
and run milk through a
column packed with them.

11
00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:37.740
Your mission: find out how a cheap paper
strip can measure the sugar in one drop

12
00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:38.530
of blood.
